<title>USA: SBC Communications Q4 shr rises 8.4 pct.</title>
<headline>SBC Communications Q4 shr rises 8.4 pct.</headline>
<text>
<p>SAN ANTONIO, Texas, Jan 21 (Reuter)</p>
<p>				1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr			  $0.90		    $0.83</p>
<p> Net		     $542,900		  505,200</p>
<p> Revs		  $3,768,400		3,442,500</p>
<p> Avg shrs		 602,100		  609,700</p>
<p>Note - SBC Communications Inc said year ago figures exclude a $111.5 million gain on the sale of U.K. cable operator Telewest Communications Plc, and charges of $87.5 million for corporate reorganisation and $11.4 million for debt refinancing. Including them per share earnings were $0.90 vs $0.85.  </p>
<p>First Call Q4 consensus estimate was $0.91/shr.</p>
<p>		 12 MONTHS</p>
<p>				1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr			  $3.46		    $3.08</p>
<p> Net		   $2,101,200		1,876,700</p>
<p> Revs		 $13,898,200	     12,669,700</p>
<p> Avg shrs		 607,300		  608,800</p>
<p>Note - SBC said figures exclude a year-ago non-cash charge of $2.89 billion for a change in accounting procedure to reflect a change in regulatory status. Including the charge, earnings per share were profit $3.46 vs loss $1.53.</p>
<p>All tabular data 000s except per share numbers.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsrom 212 859 1610))</p>
</text>
